    "summary": "A landmine explosion at a construction site in Beledweyne's Buundo Weyn district on Wednesday morning killed one person and wounded two others, according to local authorities. Security forces have launched an investigation into the incident.",
    "content": "At least one person was killed and two others were wounded when a landmine detonated on Wednesday morning at a construction site in the Buundo Weyn district of Beledweyne, the administrative capital of the Hiiraan region. The blast occurred as workers were reportedly setting up and repairing equipment at the site, leading to immediate casualties among those present.\n\nLocal security forces, including federal government troops and regional police, arrived at the scene shortly after the explosion and began an operation to secure the area and gather evidence. The authorities have not yet released the identities of the victims or stated whether any group has claimed responsibility for the attack.\n\nLandmines and improvised explosive devices have been a recurring threat in parts of central Somalia, particularly in areas where militant groups have been active. Beledweyne has experienced sporadic violence and security incidents in recent years, often linked to the broader conflict between the federal government and insurgent forces.\n\nFor the Somali diaspora, this incident underscores the persistent insecurity that affects daily life in many regions of the country, even as efforts toward stabilization continue. Family members abroad often follow such news closely, concerned for relatives who remain in areas where explosive remnants of war and planted devices pose hidden dangers to civilians.\n\nAuthorities are urging residents to report any suspicious objects and to stay alert while authorities work to dismantle potential threats. The investigation into Wednesday's blast is ongoing, and further details may emerge as security forces piece together the circumstances behind the attack.\n\nRead the original report from Goobjoog here: https://goobjoog.com/2026/09/09/qarax-miino-oo-beledweyne-ku-dilay-hal-qof-laba-kalena-dhaawacay/",
